From 1f8eaa852f3d3624ed076bf14bf86b793d8ab2ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMDR42 Closure <closure@webpent.local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:42:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] =?UTF-8?q?fix(umdr42=20A1):=20scope=20revocation=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?integrity=20=E2=80=94=204=20P1=20defects=20closed?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P1-SCOPE-REVIVE: store.clear() now tombstones EVERY active version;
current()/current_version()/redacted() pick the latest version FIRST,
then honour its tombstone — a revoked v2 can no longer resurrect v1.
P1-SCOPE-API-500: /api/v1/scope/{load,check,list,clear} map
ScopeStoreUnavailable to HTTP 503 (retryable authority-unavailable),
not an opaque 500.
P1-SCOPE-WORKER-INIT: Celery worker consumes the same
WEBPENT_SCOPE_STORE_* opt-in env contract as the API and attaches the
durable store at import (fail-closed on init failure).
P1-SCOPE-COMPOSE-ENV: docker-compose.yml passes
WEBPENT_SCOPE_STORE_{ENABLED,PATH} + shared scope-store volume to both
api and worker.

Tests: tests/test_umdr42_scope_closure.py — all four defects proven
RED on the 5a7e511c baseline before the fix, GREEN after (7/7).
Scope regression suites unchanged (69 passed). One pre-existing
failure (tests/appsuite/test_discovery.py::test_requisitions_multi_
observation_confirms_scoped_defect) reproduced on the CLEAN baseline —
not caused by this change; tracked in the closure report.

A0: deliverables/umdr42_closure/UMDR42_BASELINE_AUDIT.{json,md} —
programmatic baseline facts (BUILD_INFO provenance defects, ruff
5689 vs published-CI 8175, accounting gap -1).
